  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Consider a multiset SSS and a positive integer XXX. Suppose we partition SSS into LLL non-empty subsets such that each element of SSS is present in **exactly one** subset.\n\nThe cost of such partition is ∑i=1LX+\\sum_{i=1}^L X +∑i=1L​X+ `max`i−_i - i​− `min`i_ii​, where `max`i_ii​ and `min`i_ii​ denote the maximum and minimum elements of the i−i-i−th subset respectively.\n\nLet F(S,X)F(S, X)F(S,X) denote the minimum cost required if we partition SSS optimally.\n\nYou are given integers N,M,D,N, M, D, N,M,D, and KKK.\n\nCount the total number of multisets AAA such that:\n\n\nAAA consists of NNN elements;\n1≤Ai≤M1\\le A_i \\le M1≤Ai​≤M for all 1≤i≤N1\\le i \\le N1≤i≤N;\nF(A,D)=KF(A, D) = KF(A,D)=K.\nNote that as we are considering multisets, {1,2,2}\\{1, 2, 2 \\}{1,2,2} and {2,2,1} \\{2, 2, 1 \\}{2,2,1} are same and should be counted only once.\n\nSince the total number of multisets can be huge, please output it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of four positive integers NNN, MMM, DDD and KKK, size of multiset AAA, limit on maximum value of multiset AAA, parameter DDD and required cost KKK.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, total number of valid multisets modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103",
      "1≤N≤1031 \\leq N \\leq 10^31≤N≤103",
      "1≤M,D,K≤2⋅1061 \\leq M, D, K \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^61≤M,D,K≤2⋅106",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 5⋅1035 \\cdot 10^35⋅103.",
      "The sum of MMM over all test cases won't exceed 5⋅1065 \\cdot 10^65⋅106."
    ],
