        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The only multiset that satisfies the conditions is {1,3}\\{1, 3\\}{1,3}.\nWe can partition the multiset into two subsets {1}\\{1\\}{1} and {3}\\{3\\}{3}.\nThe cost of partition is (2+0−0)+(2+0−0)=4(2+0-0) + (2+0-0) = 4(2+0−0)+(2+0−0)=4.\nWe can also partition it into single subset {1,3}\\{1, 3 \\}{1,3}, which yields the same cost.\nTest case 222: The multisets that satisfy the conditions are {1,1,3},{1,3,3},{1,2,3}\\{1, 1, 3\\}, \\{1, 3, 3\\}, \\{1, 2, 3\\}{1,1,3},{1,3,3},{1,2,3}.\nConsider the multiset {1,2,3}\\{1, 2, 3\\}{1,2,3}. We can partition the multiset into single subset {1,2,3}\\{1, 2, 3\\}{1,2,3}.\nThe cost of partition is (2+3−1)=4(2+3-1) = 4(2+3−1)=4.\nTest case 333: It can be shown that there exists no multiset that satisfies the conditions."
